> Yes. I inspected the actual auraecosystem/Q-lang source structure. The project is already pointing toward a language/runtime, but several pieces are currently disconnected.

• The most important finding is that Lang/.ebnf defines only a small grammar around statements, assignments, calls, identifiers, numbers, and strings.  Meanwhile, Engine/Q_runtime.opy expects a QParser and QEngine and already recognizes higher-level operations such as detect, analyze, run, and define.

• The AI layer is currently a lightweight semantic layer with explain, infer, and summarize operations.  The agent subsystem is more developed: QLangAgentEngine loads an MCP registry, ingests semantic objects, and exposes an orchestration/verification interface.  The blockchain side already contains consensus and bridge components.

>> So I would build Q-lang in this direction:

